/P 75 0 R
/T (Popular Cryptocurrencies)
/E (Popular Cryptocurrencies)
/Pg 13 0 R
/K [0]
>>
endobj
99 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 75 0 R
/E (There are thousands of cryptocurrencies and digital tokens, but some have become particularly well known. Bitcoin \(BTC\) is the first and most widely recognized cryptocurrency. It was designed primarily as a peer-to-peer digital payment system and is often discussed as a digital asset or store of value. Ethereum \(ETH\) is another major cryptocurrency, but its blockchain is also designed to support smart contracts and decentralized applications. Ethereum therefore plays an important role in the wider blockchain ecosystem. BNB is the native token associated with the BNB Chain ecosystem and is used for various activities within that network. Solana \(SOL\) is another major blockchain project known for supporting decentralized applications and digital assets. These cryptocurrencies differ in their technology, design, transaction systems, and intended uses. It is important to understand that popularity does not mean that a cryptocurrency is automatically safe or profitable.Cryptocurrency prices can change significantly over short periods because of market conditions, investor sentiment, technological developments, and other factors. These examples can be used to show that the cryptocurrency ecosystem contains different types of blockchain networks rather than one single form of digital currency.)
/Pg 13 0 R
/K [1]
>>
endobj
