103 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 76 0 R
/E (Blockchain is one of the most important technologies behind cryptocurrency. It can be understood as a distributed digital ledger that records transactions in an organized and verifiable way. Instead of storing the complete transaction record in only one central location, a blockchain can maintain copies across many computers participating in the network. Transactions are grouped into blocks, and these blocks are connected to earlier blocks, creating a chain of records. Cryptographic methods help protect the integrity of the information stored on the blockchain. When a new transaction is submitted, the network follows its rules to determine whether the transaction should be accepted and recorded. Different blockchain networks use different consensus mechanisms and technical designs. One important feature of blockchain is transparency:depending on the network, transaction records can often be viewed publicly. At the same time, blockchain addresses do not necessarily directly reveal the real-world identity of their owners. Blockchain technology is not limited to cryptocurrency. It is also being explored for areas such as supply-chain tracking, digital identity, financial applications, and decentralized applications. However, blockchains also have limitations, including scalability challenges, transaction costs, energy considerations for some consensus mechanisms, and technical complexity. Understanding blockchain is therefore essential for )
/Pg 14 0 R
/K [1]
>>
endobj
