107 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 77 0 R
/E (Cryptocurrency works through a combination of blockchain technology, cryptography, digital wallets, and a network of computers. When a person wants to send cryptocurrency, they create a transaction using a wallet. The transaction contains information such as the destination address and the amount being transferred. The transaction is then broadcast to the relevant blockchain network. Network participants verify the transaction according to that blockchain's rules. Once accepted, the transaction is included in the blockchain's record. It briefly explains that cryptocurrency uses blockchain technology, is stored through digital wallets, has transactions verified by a computer network, and can be traded through cryptocurrency exchanges.Digital signatures and cryptographic keys help demonstrate that the person initiating a transaction has the necessary authority over the relevant funds. Once a transaction has been confirmed and recorded, changing it can be difficult depending on the blockchain's design. The exact process differs between cryptocurrencies because different networks use different technical systems. Some use mining-based consensus mechanisms, while others use different approaches such as proof-of-stake. Therefore, cryptocurrency does not simply mean sending )
/Pg 15 0 R
/K [1]
>>
endobj
