/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 78 0 R
/E (A cryptocurrency wallet is a tool used to manage the information needed to access and control cryptocurrency assets. It is important to understand that cryptocurrencies themselves are generally recorded on the blockchain; a wallet primarily manages the cryptographic keys or credentials that allow a person to authorize transactions. Wallets can be broadly categorized into hot wallets and cold wallets. Hot wallets are connected to the internet and are generally convenient for regular transactions. Cold wallets are kept offline or with limited online exposure and are often used when users want to reduce certain online security risks. Wallets can also exist as mobile applications, desktop software, browser-based tools, or dedicated hardware devices. A wallet normally involves a public address that can be shared when receiving funds and a private key or recovery information that must be protected.Losing access to important wallet credentials can result in losing access to the associated assets. Similarly, sharing private keys or recovery phrases can allow someone else to control the assets. Therefore, wallet security is an important part of cryptocurrency usage. Users should be careful with )
/Pg 16 0 R
/K [1]
>>
endobj
