/P 80 0 R
/E (Cryptocurrency exchanges are online platforms where users can buy, sell, or trade cryptocurrencies and other digital assets. An exchange can provide a marketplace that connects buyers and sellers and may offer different trading features. Some exchanges allow users to purchase cryptocurrency using traditional currencies, while others primarily support trading between different digital assets. Exchanges may also provide services such as price information, transaction history, and wallet functionality. However, users should understand the difference between keeping cryptocurrency on an exchange and controlling it through a personal wallet. When assets remain on a centralized exchange, the exchange generally controls the relevant private keys or custody arrangements.This creates additional risks if the platform experiences hacking, operational problems, fraud, or regulatory action. Exchanges also differ in their security practices, available services, fees, and regulatory requirements. Before using )
/Pg 18 0 R
/K [1]
>>
