139 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 83 0 R
/E (Cryptocurrency has developed beyond simple digital payment systems into several different categories of blockchain applications. Stablecoins are digital tokens designed to maintain a relatively stable value compared with a reference asset, often a traditional currency such as the US dollar. They are commonly used within cryptocurrency markets and blockchain applications. Decentralized Finance \(DeFi\) refers to financial applications built using blockchain technology and smart contracts. DeFi applications can provide services such as exchanging digital assets, lending, borrowing, and other financial activities without relying on the same centralized intermediaries used in traditional finance.However, DeFi applications can involve significant technical, financial, and security risks.)
/Pg 21 0 R
/K [1]
>>
endobj
140 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 83 0 R
/E (and regulatory environment differs between countries and can change over time. Some blockchain networks may also experience scalability problems or high transaction fees during periods of heavy demand. Another concern is that cryptocurrency systems can be technically complex, making them difficult for beginners to understand. These disadvantages show why cryptocurrency should not be treated as a guaranteed investment or risk-free form of money. A balanced understanding of cryptocurrency requires considering both its technological benefits and the financial, security, legal, and operational risks involved.)
/Pg 21 0 R
/K [2]
>>
